laude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": null, "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 9656, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 9656, "cached_input": 11816, "input": 21474, "output": 131}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 18504, "other": 423, "system": 28293, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 0}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 61617}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "fb978398-b19e-51ff-8339-361b1c9f356c", "at": 1795623634.6114435, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 8494, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12ae19cd1b930b6e4ba60b0e68ddbc5b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "bc571cbc-73eb-5760-93f4-efcc67c69212", "at": 1795623634.616891, "until": 1795623637.4512439, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 8495, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12ae19cd1b930b6e4ba60b0e68ddbc5b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01TrSRZQ1m9Mbbxt1g8ABTA9", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian && rm -rf srw && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" srw 2>&1 | tail -2; wc -c srw/Outline.md; cat srw/Outline.md", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian && rm -rf srw && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" srw 2>&1 | tail -2; wc -c srw/Outline.md; cat srw/Outline.md"]], "output": "```console\n15609 srw/Outline.md\n# Outline: which k benchmarks to run, and how well do they predict the rest?\n\n(Outline revision 2, after the review in `story-repo`#3; revision 1 was the first draft. Built from the `Brief` of idea-repo, revision 3 (2026-11-25 16:08 UTC). It says what to test, not what a result must be. Thresholds, definitions and hypotheses H1-H4 are the Brief's and are not restated in full; where this page names one, the Brief governs.)\n\n## 1. The story in one paragraph\nEvaluating a new model on N benchmarks is costly; leaderboards hold a history matrix of M models x N benchmarks. An evaluator can run only k benchmarks and wants the other N-k scores. Prior work shrinks the items *inside* one benchmark, or shows that benchmark scores are low-dimensional, but does not treat \"which k to run\" as a design problem, give a k-versus-error law, or test the answer where it matters: for a new family or a newer, stronger model. We (i) set up a leakage-free, family-clustered, paired protocol for this question; (ii) give a closed-form k-curve for a linear-Gaussian latent-factor model and check it in three tiers; (iii) compare greedy Bayesian A-optimal selection with random and standard selectors under a fixed predictor grid; and (iv) report honestly how much of the answer survives family/time shift and in which data regimes. The method is a known toolkit (PPCA/EM + Gaussian conditioning + greedy A-optimal); the contribution is the protocol, the finding, and the verified theory, in that order.\n\n**Headline claim (to be set by results; wording fixed only after H2/H3).** The paper is built around the primary result: error and closure C(k) as a function of k on real matrices, under family-held-out evaluation. The selector is *not* the headline unless it beats random under shift by the Brief's margin. Three headline forms are all acceptable, and the data choose: (A) \"informed selection beats random clearly\"; (B) \"random is nearly as good, and coherence explains why\"; (C) \"a dominant general factor means k = 1-2 gives most of it, the rest is slow\".\n\n## 2. Paper structure (main text; page budget set by `venue-repo`)\n1. **Abstract / Introduction.** The evaluator's problem; the gap (items-within-benchmark vs which-benchmarks; predictability without design; matrix completion with random observation); contributions in the Brief's order (protocol + finding, k-curve law + validity regime, honest comparison with random incl. coherence theory, method stated as known toolkit). One summary figure (Fig. 1 below).\n2. **Related work** (from `idea-repo/prior_work.md` sections A-D): A efficient single-benchmark evaluation; B cross-benchmark predictability and agreement; C matrix completion; D choosing what to observe (cold-start, CUR, sensor placement, submodularity ratio). Each paragraph ends with \"what differs here\".\n3. **Problem and protocol.** Setting; dense pool P, target set R = P \\ S fixed across all methods; grouped K-fold by family as main split, random K-fold/LOMO and time-forward as secondary; no leakage (fit on train fold, then select, then predict); paired grid; unit of replication = family; metrics (a)-(e). Pre-registered definitions (r_eff, C(k), k*, H1 outcome names, H2 single primary test, H4 tolerance).\n4. **Method.** PPCA/EM with missing data and a floor on D; Gaussian conditioning; greedy A-optimal selection; costs and applicability. Short; baselines listed in a table (appendix details).\n5. **Theory.** Risk(S) = tr(W_R Sigma_post W_R^T) + tr(D_R); k-curve as a sum over factors (equal incoherent loadings only as special case); when random is near greedy (coherence, matrix Chernoff; constants taken from the source, not memory); greedy guarantee via submodularity ratio gamma computed on each real matrix. Derivations in the appendix; statements and the regime of validity in the text.\n6. **Experiments.** Data and regimes (MTEB = idiosyncratic D; HELM MMLU = binomial-noise D; not pooled; LLM union matrix only as sparse-history study\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "938b4233-f8a8-58b0-be9d-0cdf2b483d8c", "at": 1795623635.4783695, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 8547, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12ae19cd1b930b6e4ba60b0e68ddbc5b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "ea757950-5dfa-5cbc-ab49-c3cc1060d68a", "at": 1795623635.4854438, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 8548, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12ae19cd1b930b6e4ba60b0e68ddbc5b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "8a20759d-3ff1-519e-ab47-9082fc0faf3f", "at": 1795623635.4881449, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 8549, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12ae19cd1b930b6e4ba60b0e68ddbc5b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "502fcfbc-42be-5691-9252-07ee1955d0e4", "at": 1795623635.6096597, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 8550, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "12ae19cd1b930b6e4ba60b0e68ddbc5b", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "credential challenge GET /world/story-repo.wiki.git/info/refs"}, {"id": "f7e2604b-5b5c-551c-915e-455c6d074786", "at": 1795623636.9494047, "until": 1795623636.9753525, "cloc